@* What a list says when it holds nothing — and, more to the point, what to do about it.

   Six of these read "None yet.", "None." or "Nothing yet.": a full stop reporting a fact the
   reader can already see, on the one screen where they most need telling what happens next.
   An empty list is the moment a tool is least useful and most able to help, and every one of
   them spent it restating the emptiness.

   It is a component rather than a class applied six times for the reason the rest of them are:
   one owner per repeated class, so the treatment cannot drift between six copies. It also
   gives the guard something to find — `EveryEmptyStateNamesTheNextAction` renders each editor
   with an empty character, locates this element and refuses a sentence that is only a
   negation. A class spread by hand across six files would have to be enumerated instead, and
   an enumeration is a list that goes stale. *@

<p class="empty-state small muted">@ChildContent</p>

@code {
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
